=== FINDING ===
Prompt 15 asks to verify api_call_logs.request_payload and api_call_logs.response_payload
are jsonb columns with COMMENT ON COLUMN referencing ADR-001.

Actual schema state (per migration 000142_baseline_typed.up.sql, lines 1354-1386):
  * api_call_logs has NO request_payload or response_payload columns.
  * Columns present: id, ts, vehicle_id, service, http_method, endpoint,
    status_code, duration_ms, error_message, rate_limited.
  * Table COMMENT states:
      "Append-only outbound API call log. ADR-005: no raw_json bodies;
       URL+status+duration only."
  * The table is explicitly body-free by ADR-005 design.

=== RECONCILIATION ===
ADR-001 (jsonb policy): typed-by-default; jsonb requires a named ADR carve-out.
ADR-005 (no raw_json): tesla_*.raw_json columns are deleted entirely; no request
or response bodies are persisted in audit/observability tables.

The prompt's premise (api_call_logs payload jsonb carveouts referencing ADR-001)
directly contradicts ADR-005 as implemented. Adding jsonb payload columns here
would:
  (a) violate ADR-005 (no raw_json bodies), and
  (b) break the ADR-001 invariant asserted in automation_actions.command_params:
      "Audit query SELECT count(*) FROM information_schema.columns WHERE data_type
       IN ('jsonb','json') must return exactly 1, and that 1 must be this column."

Phase 3 / baseline 000142 owns api_call_logs shape. The authoritative jsonb
carveout under ADR-001 remains automation_actions.command_params (verified in
phase-9-14-carveout-audit-log.log step 3).

Acceptance interpretation (matches phase 9.14 reconciliation pattern):
  * The carveout described by prompt 15 does NOT exist and MUST NOT exist.
  * No change to api_call_logs is warranted — adding payload jsonb columns would
    violate ADR-001 and ADR-005 simultaneously.
  * The ADR-001 invariant (exactly one jsonb column: automation_actions.command_params)
    is preserved.

